kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Envelope-changing revision, approved by the user: one check meaning change at the
  reviewed_impl_to_hardware edge, and one budget rule stated at execute_attempt_loop
  (where the count is kept), at the hardware_attempt_counts state field (where its
  meaning is declared), and mirrored at the realize_increment allowed effect.
  4 hunks, 13 added lines against 4 removed. Counts unchanged:
  32 nodes, 96 edges, 17 checks, 89 outcomes.

  (a) THE PRE-HARDWARE REVIEW CHECK ADMITS NON-PRODUCT COMMITS
  (impl_commit_is_reviewed). Before: the worktree commit had to equal the commit the
  adversarial review stamped, so a lane that repaired its own test, control, launcher,
  checker or bundle after the review (revision 8 gave it that authority) lost
  ready_for_hardware and waited for a new review of a change that touched no product
  source. Now the check also passes when every commit after the stamped one changes
  only tests, controls, launchers, checkers or bundles and no product source, each
  named with its file set in the attempt log; a product-source commit still fails the
  check and re-enters review_implementation.

  (b) A CPU-MODE RUN IS NOT A HARDWARE ATTEMPT ON ANY HOST (execute_attempt_loop
  purpose, hardware_attempt_counts meaning, realize_increment allowed effect). The
  per-target budget (hardware_attempt_counts) counts non-host-level failures of
  hardware attempts in execute_attempt_loop and budget-counted venv-recipe retries in
  replicate_campaign_venv. A CPU-mode run (VLLM_NEURON_CPU_MODE=1) opens no Neuron
  device; the clause removes the reading that charged such runs on the leased host
  to that budget, and states it where the counter is read so a stage-7 lead cannot
  read the stage-6 sentence as not governing the loop.

  FIELD EVIDENCE: (a) the campaign's lanes repaired launchers after review and waited
  for a lead word the graph never required (ceremony audit 2026-09-10; user ruling
  recorded at 2026-09-10T17:05:11Z in the campaign log); (b) the campaign log counted ten
  CPU-mode launches on the leased host as budget attempts and tripped the breaker on
  them, a reading the plan never intended. Both
  drafted in the 1.5.5 batch, withheld for the user's word, and approved by the user
  on 2026-09-10 in answer to two plain questions (recorded verbatim in the approval).
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 9 (graph): impl_commit_is_reviewed also passes when the commits after the
  reviewed one change only tests, controls, launchers, checkers or bundles and no
  product source; a CPU-mode run that opens no Neuron device is not a hardware
  attempt on any host and never increments hardware_attempt_counts. 32 nodes, 96 edges, 17 checks, 89 outcomes; 13 added lines against
  4 removed in 4 hunks. Approved by the user 2026-09-10 ("a. yes b. yes").
